/-!
# verify_counter: the assembly stage of looping code at every gas

solar's final EVM IR of solar-verify's Counter (`SolarTV.Export.Counter.evm11`, after
`loop-layout`) has the loop of `bump` (blocks 7 and 8, with the back edge from block 7 to
block 8). `Assemble.check` bounds runs by a static potential and so rejects it; the checker of
code with loops accepts it (`check_ok`, the kernel's evaluation), and `within_of_checkL` gives
the stage `Final.compose_anyGas` needs: at every gas, every result of the 496-byte runtime
is the EVM IR's or a failure that changes nothing, on every call, under every oracle.

`loopTarget_check`: the bytecode whose back edge jumps to block 7's JUMPDEST in place of block
8's (byte 168) is rejected: its walk decodes a push of 0xaa where the layout puts block 8 at
0xdb.
-/

namespace SolidCore.Refinement.Solar.VerifyCounterAsm

open SolidCore.Refinement.Solar.Assemble SolidCore.Refinement.Solar.AssembleLoop

